---
// The privacy page's text in English. Its layout and styles are in
// src/pages/[lang]/privacy.astro; every language needs its own file here.
import { contactEmail, owner } from "../../../data/site";

// The page passes `lang`, like the other page texts; this text needs no link that depends on it.
export interface Props {
  lang: string;
}
---

<p class="updated">Last updated: 3 November 2026</p>

<p class="lead">
  Handball Coachboard sets no cookies and has no accounts. Your boards stay on your device until
  you share them.
</p>

<h2>Who runs this site</h2>
<p>
  Handball Coachboard is run by {owner}. Questions about your privacy? Email <a
    href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a
  >. We only use your address and your message to reply to you.
</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>
  This site sets no cookies, first-party or third-party. There are no ads either. That's why there
  is no cookie banner.
</p>

<h2>The board</h2>
<p>
  Your boards are kept in your browser's storage, on your own device. They only leave your device
  when you share them yourself, as a link or as a file.
</p>
<p>
  In a shared link, the drawing sits after the <code>#</code> in the address. Your browser doesn't
  send that part to any server. That means we don't see what you draw. Your browser also makes the
  QR code itself.
</p>

<h2>Hosting</h2>
<p>
  The site runs on Cloudflare. To deliver pages and protect the site against abuse, Cloudflare
  processes technical data, such as your IP address and your browser. Every web server does that.
  We don't use that data to identify you. See the <a
    href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
    rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a
  >.
</p>
<p>
  In Cloudflare's dashboard we see totals only: how many requests and visitors the site gets. The
  site loads no statistics script and no other script from outside. We don't see what you draw.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>When something changes, we update this page and the date at the top.</p>
